As a Project Manager , you will be responsible for overseeing the entire project&nbsp;life-cycle, from initiation to completion, and ensuring that all project goals, objectives, and deliverables are met on time and within budget. Responsibilities include submitting project deliverables, preparing status reports, and establishing effective project communication plans as well as the proper execution of said plans. The successful candidate will work directly with clients to ensure deliverables fall within the applicable scope and budget. He or she will coordinate with other departments to ensure all aspects of each project are compatible. &nbsp;

WHO WE’RE LOOKING FOR: &nbsp;

We’re looking for a&nbsp; Project Manager &nbsp;to support fast-paced digital work across creative production and web development. This is a hands-on delivery role for someone with proven experience managing day-to-day coordination in fast-paced environments, while working closely with senior creative and engineering leads. You bring structure to SOWs and timelines, communicate with clarity, and keep work moving smoothly across teams. Strong data awareness, BI fluency, and cross-functional collaboration are essential. &nbsp;

WHAT YOU’LL DO: &nbsp;

• Manage the day-to-day execution of digital projects across creative production and web development &nbsp;

• Support senior leads by tracking progress, maintaining timelines, and keeping project plans up to date &nbsp;

• Coordinate with design, development, QA, and content teams to align deliverables and remove bottlenecks &nbsp;

• Communicate clearly with clients and internal stakeholders to clarify requirements and share timely updates &nbsp;

• Prepare documentation, status reports, and meeting notes that keep everyone aligned &nbsp;

• Monitor quality across deliverables and ensure each handoff meets expectations &nbsp;

• Flag risks early and help maintain delivery momentum across multiple workstreams &nbsp;

• Contribute to team-wide improvements in reporting, tracking, and workflow efficiency &nbsp;

WHAT YOU’LL NEED: &nbsp;

• 4+ years of experience managing digital projects or production workflows, ideally within a digital agency, SaaS, or ITES environment &nbsp;

• Exposure to both creative production (banners, motion, video) and web development (UI/UX, front-end, back-end) &nbsp;

• Practical understanding of Agile and Scrum, with hands-on experience using tools like Jira, Wrike, or Trello &nbsp;

• Clear, confident communication skills, with the ability to coordinate across functions and manage client expectations &nbsp;

